messages:
alex_k: Quick follow-up to the fused-attention RFC — propose a small runtime adapter layer so we can ship multiple fused variants safely without changing the operator contract.

alex_k: tl;dr: attach a per-model capabilities bitset (fused_qkv, fused_bias_rope, dropoutless_infer) and an AdapterRegistry that rewrites request buffers at enqueue time when the kernel expects a different layout. keep a no-op adapter when model and kernel match.

maria_g: +1. low-risk approach. we need to surface adapter cost in telemetry (cpu/gpu ms, extra mem) so we know when translations are expensive.

samir: must preserve KV-cache absolute offsets and ROPE semantics. adapters can change buffer layout but not the meaning of offsets used by resumed generations.

ria_ops: ops concern: router mixing. if canary nodes use fused_qkv and fallback nodes don't, the router may batch incompatible layouts. we need router pinning or a runtime batch compatibility check.

alex_k: rollout plan idea: pin model variant per deployment (canary group only), router annotations so we avoid mixing, and a runtime batch check that rejects mixed-layout batches.

maria_g: API sketch for AdapterRegistry:
```
// register at startup
AdapterRegistry::register("pack_qkv_v3", Adapter::make_qkv_packer(params));

// runtime enqueue
KernelRunner::enqueue(request) {
  if (!request.model.supports(kernel.expected_caps)) {
    adapter = AdapterRegistry::find(kernel.expected_caps);
    adapter->transform(request.buffers);
  }
  kernel->run(request.buffers);
}
```

samir: small perf note: annotate adapters with `graph_compatible` and `temp_mem_bytes`. some transforms can be fused into cuda graphs; others need dynamic kernels.

maria_g: propose test matrix: baseline (no fusion), fused_qkv only, fused_bias_rope only, fused_qkv + fused_bias_rope, and dropoutless_infer. for each: throughput/latency, memory, kv-cache-consistency, and token-level logits diff smoke tests.

ria_ops: telemetry we should add: adapter_applied (bool), adapter_name (string), transform_cpu_ms, transform_gpu_ms, extra_mem_bytes, kernel_tag. console should show these on per-request traces.

alex_k: rollout guardrails idea: if adapter_applied and transform_gpu_ms > 3x baseline median, auto-disable that variant. also auto-rollback if QoE error rate > 0.5% vs baseline.

samir: on dropoutless inference: need semantic tests. some models rely on implicit dropout regularization during training; for inference we must ensure fused dropoutless paths don't change RNG/determinism or softmax numerics. add perplexity/token-divergence tests.

maria_g: I'll add a nightly CI job that runs the adapter test matrix and a small QoE smoke harness that reports token-level divergence thresholds.

ria_ops: UI/ops items: surface model capability flags on the model page and in rollout UI; support search by capability (capabilities:fused_qkv). runbook should include per-host force-disable switch and router pinning steps.

alex_k: next actions: PR AdapterRegistry + minimal qkv_packer adapter (alex_k); perf microbenchmarks + telemetry spike (samir); tests/test_adapters.py harness and QoE smoke (maria_g); rollout plan doc and router pinning implementation (ria_ops).

build-bot: CI pipeline triggered for repo:redwood/serve (job: adapter-spike).

alex_k: thanks all — priority is keeping the adapter small, observable, and revokable. if you hit edge-cases (mixed-head models, variable head sizes, odd kv-cache layouts) drop notes here and we can triage.
